@echo off
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE WHILE IT IS RUNNING. NOT EVEN A COMMENT.
rem
rem cmd.exe reads a batch file INCREMENTALLY, BY BYTE OFFSET, as it executes
rem it. Changing the file's length mid-run moves everything after the cursor,
rem and execution resumes at an offset that no longer means what it meant.
rem
rem That cost INFRA-VIEWER-001 a four-hour qualification that had PASSED: two
rem minutes in, a comment was reworded; four hours later, when qualify.cmd
rem returned, cmd.exe resumed at a stale offset and called it a SECOND time,
rem truncating qualification-times.txt and overwriting three of debug-ext's
rem logs. The run had already printed "every stage exited 0" and the evidence
rem for it was gone.
rem
rem EVERY LINE OF THIS FILE BEGINS WITH rem, set, call, echo, setlocal,
rem endlocal OR @echo, AND THAT IS CHECKED BEFORE THE RUN.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem
rem P17-CLI-001 HEADLESS STRUCTURAL FEA. The exact invocation, recorded so the
rem run is reproducible rather than described.
rem
rem qualify.cmd is byte-identical to the one P16-SIZE-001 settled on and every
rem milestone since has used, TWENTY-NINE in a row counting this one.
rem
rem   qualify.cmd          git hash-object d313a64070718c44fae290ac042fe259d1a03c8b
rem                        sha1sum         244b38de8feac0475af7cdc56ba9415d27d8dd29
rem   verify-harness.cmd   git hash-object 11855b8ff891093b021d1e0351761283d0eedd24
rem                        sha1sum         afd0197d4f4726db7f533c2f27f4f6e069ba83c6
rem
rem BOTH FORMS ARE RECORDED because they differ and a hash without its
rem algorithm cannot be checked: .gitattributes sets `*.cmd text eol=crlf`, so
rem git stores LF while the working tree is CRLF.
rem
rem CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6, carried for the reason INFRA-VIEWER-001
rem recorded: 16 logical cores let `cmake --build` run 18 compiles at once, and
rem a CLEAN build of over 600 template-heavy translation units exhausted the
rem commit charge. Capping parallelism weakens nothing -- same sources, same
rem flags, -Werror included. ctest stays at -j 8.
rem
rem WHAT THE AUDIT FOUND, AND WHY THIS MILESTONE ADDS NO ARCHITECTURE. Every
rem question the brief raises about command style, exit codes, mutation
rem semantics, output channels, unit parsing, backend suppression, the
rem fresh-binary proof and zero-match protection already had an answer in the
rem tree with a recorded reason:
rem
rem   the edit spine (ADR-009)   a mutation is a function over an ALREADY
rem                              LOADED document, and ONE registration makes
rem                              it both a single-shot command and a batch
rem                              verb, with nothing added to BatchCommand.cpp
rem   exit codes                 THREE since P10 -- Success, Failure,
rem                              UsageError -- with the granularity in the
rem                              diagnostic CODE, which is P15-CLI-001's
rem                              design: "only the code is an interface"
rem   structured output          JsonValue, --json, and quantity(value, unit)
rem                              whose comment is the rule: "NEVER A BARE
rem                              NUMBER"
rem   the face grammar           parseFaceReference, shared with datums,
rem                              drafts, dimensions, mates and local sizing
rem   the quantity parser        parseQuantity, dimension-generic ON PURPOSE
rem                              so a new quantity "cannot acquire a second
rem                              spelling, a second unit table or a second
rem                              dimension check"
rem   Netgen's stdout            ALREADY contained in the adapter, by
rem                              P16-CLI-001, which found it the hard way
rem   fresh-binary proof         structural: $<TARGET_FILE:bettercad_cli>
rem   zero-match protection      ZeroMatchGuard.cmake, with its own self-proof
rem
rem SO THIS RUN ADDS ELEVEN COMMANDS AND NO ARCHITECTURE. Six reports and five
rem edits, following P16's ten mesh-* commands exactly -- six reports and four
rem edits -- and NOT ONE FILE under src/ or include/ changed.
rem
rem WHAT CHANGED SINCE 7e18175.
rem
rem   NEW          apps/bettercad_cli/StructuralEdits.cpp
rem                              Five edits. Each is an adapter: parse, resolve
rem                              a selector, build the P17-CMD command, hand it
rem                              to execute(). No rule of any kind in the file.
rem                apps/bettercad_cli/StructuralReports.cpp
rem                              Six reports. One shared solve() helper, so
rem                              solve and the three summaries cannot drift
rem                              about which refusals apply.
rem                tests/cli/StructuralCliTests.cpp
rem                              19 cases. EVERY engineering assertion is an
rem                              equivalence against the core; there is no
rem                              expected-value table.
rem                tests/cli/StructuralWorkflow.cmake
rem                              28 steps, 28 PROCESSES, every payload parsed
rem                              with string(JSON) -- a real parser, so
rem                              contamination is fatal rather than filtered.
rem
rem   MODIFIED     apps/bettercad_cli/Commands.hpp        6 usages, 6 decls
rem                apps/bettercad_cli/Cli.cpp             6 dispatch rows
rem                apps/bettercad_cli/Edits.hpp           1 declaration
rem                apps/bettercad_cli/EditRegistry.cpp    1 table joined
rem                apps/bettercad_cli/CMakeLists.txt      2 sources, 1 link
rem                tests/CMakeLists.txt                   1 source, 9 process
rem                                                       tests, 1 workflow
rem                tests/cli/ZeroMatchGuard.cmake         2 filters
rem
rem NO CORE MODULE CHANGED, so NO PREDECESSOR IS REQUALIFIED. In particular
rem the Netgen adapter is untouched: its SilentBackendScope already contains
rem the backend's stdout chatter, and the brief's §206 requalification clause
rem therefore does not apply. What this run DOES re-exercise is the whole CLI
rem surface, because Cli.cpp, Commands.hpp and the edit registry are shared by
rem every command family -- so every cli.* test runs unfiltered in all three
rem presets, P16's mesh CLI included.
rem
rem THE ONE PRODUCTION DEFECT THIS MILESTONE FOUND IN ITSELF, and what found
rem it: `elementCount` is triangles PLUS tetrahedra, so a 12-tetrahedron block
rem reported 24 beside a stress range over 12 elements. The core-equivalence
rem test compared the printed count against RecoveredFields::elements().size()
rem and got 24 == 12. Both counts are now reported, named apart. A smoke test
rem asserting "some positive number" could not have seen it.
rem
rem MUTATION: 17 runs over 13 mutations, 12 killed, 1 equivalent mutant kept
rem with the tie-count MEASURED, and TWO REAL TEST GAPS closed:
rem   L5   the stress extremum's VALUE was read by nothing -- the id, the unit
rem        and the range were all compared and the one number the probe
rem        corrupted was not
rem   L10  faceResolves is written at TWO call sites, and a whole-payload
rem        substring assertion was satisfied by the restraint's `false` while
rem        the load's was hard-coded true. An assertion that was true, that
rem        passed, and that passed under the very defect it was written for.
rem One probe returned "DID NOT COMPILE -- VOID" with ZERO error: lines in its
rem log: the disk had filled and ar truncated the library to 8 bytes. The
rem restore-build gate caught it, and the probe on rerun killed three tests.
rem A void is a void.
rem
rem What IS in the repeat set, and why. THE FILTER IS UNCHANGED: `gui\.` and
rem `architecture` were already there, and the new cases are named
rem unit.StructuralCli* and cli.structural.*, which `unit\.Structural` already
rem covers as a substring for the first. The SELECTED COUNT IS RECORDED BY
rem THIS RUN rather than predicted here -- a figure nobody has measured does
rem not belong in the evidence for a run.
rem
rem compile_fail is excluded from the REPEAT for the reason the previous
rem sixteen milestones recorded: each case is a real COMPILATION, so repeating
rem one measures the compiler's determinism and not BetterCAD's. They still run
rem UNFILTERED in all three presets.
rem
rem QUALIFY_REPEAT is expanded as !REPEAT! inside qualify.cmd, never %REPEAT%:
rem a %VAR% holding | ( or ) is substituted when the for-block is PARSED and
rem closes the block early, killing the run after every preset has passed.
rem THIS RUN HAPPENED ON A SECOND MACHINE, and that is the one deviation from
rem every qualification before it. The uqhas machine that holds the build
rem root above was unavailable, so the owner decided (2026-10-14, late) to
rem stand the environment up on the hasib machine and qualify there. What is
rem identical, checked rather than assumed: GCC 16.1.0 WinLibs POSIX UCRT r4
rem (the revision INFRA-NETGEN-001 records), the CMake 4.4.1 and Ninja it
rem bundles, and the dependency prefix built by deps/CMakeLists.txt from the
rem same hash-verified archives: Qt 6.11.2, OCCT 8.0.1, zlib 1.3.1, Netgen
rem 6.2.2604. The configure summary block is identical to the uqhas machine's
rem except for paths.
rem
rem What differs, and why each is in the CACHE rather than on this line:
rem   BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT        C:/Users/hasib/bcdev/bc-build, below
rem   BETTERCAD_DEPS_PREFIX       C:/Users/hasib/bcdev/bettercad-deps/
rem                               gnu-16-mingw-amd64. The %LOCALAPPDATA%
rem                               default could not be used: a shell launched
rem                               from the packaged Claude desktop app has its
rem                               AppData\Local writes virtualised into the
rem                               app's container, which Qt's build-path check
rem                               refuses and no other shell can see.
rem   FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_*   Catch2, nlohmann_json and Eigen from
rem                               archives fetched outside CMake and verified
rem                               against the SHA256 in
rem                               cmake/BetterCADDependencies.cmake, because
rem                               the bundled CMake's curl has no CA trust
rem                               anchors (carried constraint 7, reproduced).
rem Each tree was configured once with those three -D flags before this run;
rem qualify.cmd's plain `cmake --preset` then reuses the cache, exactly as it
rem reuses the pre-existing caches on the uqhas machine.
rem
rem A debug-ext build and full ctest (3949/3949, 1768 s) preceded this run on
rem this machine, as the proof the environment works. It is not part of the
rem evidence below; only this harness run is.
setlocal
set "BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT=C:/Users/hasib/bcdev/bc-build"
set "CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6"
set "QUALIFY_PRESETS=debug-ext release-ext debug-shared-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT_PRESETS=release-ext debug-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT=architecture|unit\.Structural|unit\.Quality|unit\.MeshDofMap|unit\.ConstraintSet|unit\.FreeEquationMap|unit\.Tet4Element|unit\.Mesh|unit\.Volume|unit\.Tet|unit\.Siz|unit\.Id|unit\.ReferenceModel|unit\.Analytic|unit\.View|refmod\.|gui\.|cli\.structural\."
call "%~dp0qualify.cmd" "%~dp0."
set "RESULT=%errorlevel%"
echo qualify.cmd exit %RESULT%
endlocal & exit /b %RESULT%
